This skill is adapted from Ben Holmes's skills, skills/simplify/, and renamed `tidy`
so it doesn't collide with Claude Code's bundled `simplify`.

Upstream repository: https://github.com/bholmesdev/skills
Upstream commit: 44da67bd1896cdafced6f60573b62ae71d18ef2a
Upstream directory: https://github.com/bholmesdev/skills/tree/44da67bd1896cdafced6f60573b62ae71d18ef2a/skills/simplify

The adapted skill preserves the upstream MIT license (see LICENSE). Its description
runs it on completed changes before review or when requested, within the current
task, instead of automatically whenever code feels ready or comments come up. It
also names the diff base, keeps structural moves inside the touched code (wider
ones become suggestions), lets the repo's conventions and lenses win where
they overlap, and ends with a report and a Done when.
